WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.310
- I'm James Briscione, director
of culinary research here

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.493
at the Institute of Culinary Education.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.853
Today, we're going to make
your Big Mac meal fancy.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.220
So we're going to start
things off here with a little

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.270
French fry mousse.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.660
We took our large French fries,

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.255
blended them with a
little bit of hot milk,

00:00:24.255 --> 00:00:28.343
which makes this beautiful,
creamy, potato puree,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.770
and we're going to load that into

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.090
the whipping canister here.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.613
That's going to create a
beautiful, silky, potato mousse.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.030
Alright, so that's potato mousse.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.540
Now, ketchup caviar.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.840
I love ketchup in my burger.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.640
Ketchup can look a whole lot better.

00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:49.550
We're going to start here with
just a bit of water and agar.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.887
We're going to take that
and whisk it into the water.

00:00:51.887 --> 00:00:53.680
The reason we like agar instead of gelatin

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.883
is that because it will stay
gelled at warm temperatures,

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.463
where gelatin is going to
dissolve really quickly.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.400
So the agar and water
mixture has come to a boil.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.700
Now we just turn that down

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:06.853
and add our ketchup.

00:01:09.581 --> 00:01:12.481
Let that ketchup and agar cook
together for just a moment.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.073
So agar and ketchup mixture
in the squeeze bottle.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.150
This is where things get fun.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.083
We've got a bath of cold oil.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.080
So this is oil that's been in the freezer

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.770
and is now sitting over ice,

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.790
so it's super, super cold.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.400
So we take our hot ketchup-agar mixture,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.500
and we're going to drop
it into ice cold oil.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.163
So if we add it drop by drop,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.503
we're going to get perfect
little pearls of ketchup.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.553
Really cool little trick,

00:01:40.553 --> 00:01:42.210
you can do this with any kind of liquid,

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.700
fruit juices, and really
anything you want.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.480
Now we just scoop these guys up

00:01:47.288 --> 00:01:50.273
and drop them into a
little water to rinse,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.973
there it is, ketchup caviar.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.583
I think we're ready to plate.

00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:55.416
So here we go.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:56.702
We got our Big Mac,

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:57.649
went ahead and grabbed a plate

00:01:58.162 --> 00:01:59.390
of just some extra, kind
of typical burger toppings,

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.500
pickles, lettuce, tomato, onion.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.050
We got our mustard and ketchup.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:03.920
We're ready to go.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.325
We're actually going to start here

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.653
with a little bit of ketchup
and a little bit of mustard.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.870
You know you need that on your burger

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:11.964
right next to each other.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.030
And then, I'm going to
take a paintbrush and just

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:16.313
run that right through.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.730
Nice little base there.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:18.600
We've got our

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.873
French fry mousse.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.900
Just going to kinda drop
a little bit of that

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.023
down around the plate.

00:02:26.719 --> 00:02:27.570
That's going to just
kinda set up the frame

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.203
for our burger.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.820
Now, our Big Mac,

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:32.980
take this bad boy apart.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.500
I've got one patty with the cheese

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.723
and then another patty.

00:02:37.558 --> 00:02:38.391
So we're going to take those two guys,

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.470
slice those and just kinda frame them up,

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.440
and they're going to rest right here

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.043
between that French fry mousse.

00:02:45.311 --> 00:02:46.540
And now we're starting
to set up a little bit of

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.730
framing and a little
movement on the plate.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.760
Bun is going to give us
some nice little textures.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.110
I'm going to take that bun,

00:02:52.509 --> 00:02:53.342
actually tear it into pieces,

00:02:53.342 --> 00:02:55.733
and just drop it right around here.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.530
So now we're starting to
kinda fill out this plate.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.670
We're getting a good look.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.513
Tuck that right around there.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.190
Then our little garnishes here.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.410
So we've got our pickles

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.720
and just drop some nice
pickles right in there,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.060
love pickles so we're
going with lots of these,

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:11.163
little bit of onion,

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:14.683
tuck those right in,

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.483
love these little rings right here.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:19.460
Now a bit of our tomato,

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.420
just cut it up into some small pieces,

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.780
get some different shapes happening,

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.733
so they tuck right in.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.280
And then finish it all with
some nice fresh lettuce here,

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.213
get a nice little shape on that,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.753
just like this.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.250
Drop three of those around there.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.043
Looking really good.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.420
So our burger's plated

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.570
and then we finish it off
with my favorite piece,

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.933
that ketchup caviar.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.150
We just grab a little
bit of our caviar there,

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:49.473
and now we're going to
drop it right in there.

00:03:56.213 --> 00:03:59.296
And with ketchup caviar, there it is,

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.603
the Big Mac meal transformed.

